Z||000000||2birds||12-19-2000||07:02 PM||||I finally found a good alignment shop.  Sears in Brunswick, GA did mine for 54.95 (and they said it was the same even if I hadn't bought four new tires at the same time).  It only took the guy 2.5 hours to do it, after I explained how to adjust the front camber with my Moog ball joints.  It only took him ten tries to get the camber right, since it is hit and miss, but he stuck to it until it was right.  The car handles so much better now, and without any real bump steer, that I wonder if the last few alignments have been done right...  The car even fits on the rack without any scraping (it's lowered).||||reg||10
